# Machine-local state never enters the tree (founding spec riders; the
# committed device-id on PR #44 is the miss that earned this carrier).
.local/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# HARNESS MACHINERY, never commit material (kogaki#299). Agent worktrees are
# created and removed by the harness, and each one is a checkout of some other
# session's branch — a run that swept them into a commit would be committing
# another session's working tree. This is the same class as the block above
# rather than the repo-visible one below: nobody reads these where they work,
# they are simply state the tree should never have been offered.
.claude/worktrees/

# The Full Report's OWNER RENDERING (SPEC.md §2.5.2, SPEC-terrain §12.2 v11,
# kogaki#234). Repo-VISIBLE so the owner reads it where they work; NOT
# committed, because it derives from uncommitted survey records and inherits
# their sensitivity — visibility and publication are two decisions and this
# line is the second one, made explicitly rather than by where the file landed.
reports/

# The SHAPE READ (specs/spec-client-kit/SPEC.md §3.3, kogaki#325) — the second
# member of exactly that class, and installed by policy/kit/install.sh step 4d
# into every kit consumer. Repo-VISIBLE so every session and the owner read it
# where they work; NOT committed, because it derives from hub owner-realm
# material and this repository is public — committing it would be a
# declassification act the spec grants no grounds for.
policy/shape.md

# The MOVE-INGESTION SPECIMEN (specs/spec-draft-pipeline/SPEC.md §6.9.0,
# kogaki#223; dispositioned kogaki#299) — the THIRD member of that class, and
# the only one an owner writes by hand. §6.9.0 binds the input grammar to this
# file as its measured specimen and records it as "owner-authored, deliberately
# untracked"; this line is that clause's declaration in the carrier that
# enforces it. Repo-VISIBLE because the owner authors it where they work; NOT
# committed, because an admitted Move lands one file in `moves/` through the
# ingestion command's own review screen, and §6.9's "ADMISSION IS THE OWNER'S
# ACT AT THAT SCREEN, never the command's" is exactly what committing the input
# would route around — it would admit by location what the spec reserves for a
# gate. ANCHORED with a leading slash: the clause binds the REPOSITORY-ROOT
# file, and a bare `moves.md` would also exclude `moves/moves.md` — silently
# un-addable, which is the admission-by-omission this comment argues against.
/moves.md
